WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:01.401 --> 00:00:02.969
-I'm talking with the great
Julia Louis-Dreyfus.

00:00:02.969 --> 00:00:05.037
Julia, thanks again
for doing my show.

00:00:05.037 --> 00:00:07.640
You know, you're doing
a fundraiser tomorrow night

00:00:07.640 --> 00:00:09.909
with a couple of
your "Seinfeld" pals.

00:00:09.909 --> 00:00:13.513
Tell me about this
and how it came together.

00:00:13.513 --> 00:00:15.281
-Okay. So...
[ Clears throat ]

00:00:15.281 --> 00:00:18.617
A couple weeks ago now,
I did a fundraiser

00:00:18.617 --> 00:00:21.820
for the Wisconsin Democratic
Party with the "Veep" cast.

00:00:21.820 --> 00:00:23.790
-Yeah.
-And it went very well.

00:00:23.790 --> 00:00:26.025
It was very, very successful.

00:00:26.025 --> 00:00:30.196
And, so, I'm just
constantly racking my brain

00:00:30.196 --> 00:00:32.331
about getting the message out
about voting

00:00:32.331 --> 00:00:34.000
and raising funds
for the Democrats

00:00:34.000 --> 00:00:35.969
and what's an effective way
to doing that.

00:00:35.969 --> 00:00:38.070
I thought, "Oh, well,
let's get the 'Seinfeld'

00:00:38.070 --> 00:00:40.172
group together, if I can."
It was very last-minute.

00:00:40.172 --> 00:00:42.208
I mean, like, hyper last-minute.
-Yeah.

00:00:42.208 --> 00:00:47.046
-And we thought, "Oh, let's do
a fundraiser for Texas."

00:00:47.046 --> 00:00:49.915
Because Texas is on the verge
of turning blue.

00:00:49.915 --> 00:00:54.119
I mean, sort of all the way
down the ballot,

00:00:54.119 --> 00:00:59.359
not just congressional seats,
but also the state legislature.

00:00:59.359 --> 00:01:01.461
And that's incredibly important.
-Really?

00:01:01.461 --> 00:01:05.932
-Because if we're able to turn
the state legislature blue,

00:01:05.932 --> 00:01:09.035
then we get a seat at the table
when it comes to redistricting.

00:01:09.035 --> 00:01:11.404
And, you know, the Republicans

00:01:11.404 --> 00:01:14.774
have been very, very crafty
in their gerrymandering,

00:01:14.774 --> 00:01:18.611
which is not a cool thing to do,
and so it's important --

00:01:18.611 --> 00:01:21.013
State legislature races
in addition, of course,

00:01:21.013 --> 00:01:24.851
to the other races, are just
as important, just as critical.

00:01:24.851 --> 00:01:27.019
So we thought,
let's raise funds for Texas,

00:01:27.019 --> 00:01:29.122
'cause there's
a real opportunity here.

00:01:29.122 --> 00:01:30.289
So that's what we're doing.

00:01:30.289 --> 00:01:34.394
So, Larry David,
Jason Alexander, and myself.

00:01:34.394 --> 00:01:35.461
-Wow.

00:01:35.461 --> 00:01:36.862
-And Seth Meyers
is going to moderate.

00:01:36.862 --> 00:01:38.865
And we're going to -- Each of us
is going to talk about --

00:01:38.865 --> 00:01:40.466
We're going to
pick an episode --

00:01:40.466 --> 00:01:43.635
We have picked an episode,
each of us,

00:01:43.635 --> 00:01:45.537
to talk about sort of,

00:01:45.537 --> 00:01:47.573
I don't know, the making of,
behind the scenes,

00:01:47.573 --> 00:01:49.608
that kind of stuff.
It'll be really fun.

00:01:49.608 --> 00:01:51.210
-That's going to be great.

00:01:51.210 --> 00:01:53.312
Can you tell us
what episode you picked or no?

00:01:53.312 --> 00:01:58.617
-Yes.
I picked "The soup Nazi."

00:01:58.617 --> 00:02:02.522
And Jason Alexander picked
"The Marine Biologist."

00:02:02.522 --> 00:02:04.891
And Larry David picked
"The Contest."

00:02:04.891 --> 00:02:07.360
-[ Laughs ]
-So -- I know.

00:02:07.360 --> 00:02:09.462
So, anyway
that'll be super fun.

00:02:09.462 --> 00:02:11.797
And we're going to have
sort of "Seinfeld"

00:02:11.797 --> 00:02:14.734
memorabilia stuff --
I got, like, a --

00:02:14.734 --> 00:02:18.371
That we're going to raffle away
to people who sign up for this.

00:02:18.371 --> 00:02:21.708
And you can go to
afundraiseraboutsomething.com

00:02:21.708 --> 00:02:25.812
if you want to --
to join the party tomorrow.

00:02:25.812 --> 00:02:28.948
-Yeah. And it's important
to encourage people

00:02:28.948 --> 00:02:32.752
to talk about their voting plan,
is what you have been saying.

00:02:32.752 --> 00:02:35.320
-Oh, yes.
-Why -- Their voting plan.

00:02:35.320 --> 00:02:38.090
So it's not even like just --
Why is that important?

00:02:38.090 --> 00:02:39.992
-Well...

00:02:39.992 --> 00:02:43.696
getting people to vote
sometimes can be a heavy lift.

00:02:43.696 --> 00:02:46.766
I think sometimes because
the voter-suppression effort

00:02:46.766 --> 00:02:50.336
is such a strong one
that people feel disenfranchised

00:02:50.336 --> 00:02:52.204
and feel as if their vote
doesn't matter.

00:02:52.204 --> 00:02:54.540
But, of course, you and I
both know that's not the case.

00:02:54.540 --> 00:02:57.377
The more people vote, the better
it is for our democracy.

00:02:57.377 --> 00:02:59.111
And I do mean that, really.

00:02:59.111 --> 00:03:02.315
I say that as a Democrat.
I say it -- I believe that.

00:03:02.315 --> 00:03:05.618
And research shows us
that if you, for instance,

00:03:05.618 --> 00:03:07.720
Jimmy, talked to three
of your friends

00:03:07.720 --> 00:03:10.256
who may not be
that inclined to vote, right?

00:03:10.256 --> 00:03:12.559
And you say,
"What's your voting plan?"

00:03:12.559 --> 00:03:14.594
And they say,
"Well, I'm not sure."

00:03:14.594 --> 00:03:19.599
And you can kind of sort of talk
them into casting their ballot.

00:03:19.599 --> 00:03:21.234
You will have a very --

00:03:21.234 --> 00:03:24.637
You have a very good shot
at getting them to vote.

00:03:24.637 --> 00:03:26.805
So, in addition
to making your own plan,

00:03:26.805 --> 00:03:28.908
asking people in your life

00:03:28.908 --> 00:03:30.977
what their plan is,
is very effective.

00:03:30.977 --> 00:03:32.879
-It sparks.
-So my plan --

00:03:32.879 --> 00:03:34.414
Here's my ballot right here.

00:03:34.414 --> 00:03:36.816
I'm going to fill this out,
and I'm voting early

00:03:36.816 --> 00:03:38.984
and taking it in next week.

00:03:38.984 --> 00:03:40.286
That's my plan.

00:03:40.286 --> 00:03:42.088
-Ah!
-What's your plan?

00:03:42.088 --> 00:03:44.657
-I've sent mine in.
I handed mine to a --

00:03:44.657 --> 00:03:46.625
I went to the post office
here in the building.

00:03:46.625 --> 00:03:48.761
I did it last week.

00:03:48.761 --> 00:03:51.631
I filled out my ballot
with black ink, by the way.

00:03:51.631 --> 00:03:53.299
Black ink.
-Good.

00:03:53.299 --> 00:03:55.334
-Don't use a pencil.
Don't use colored ink.

00:03:55.334 --> 00:03:57.603
Black ink.
I did it in the secret envelope.

00:03:57.603 --> 00:03:59.772
I put the secret envelope
in the other envelope

00:03:59.772 --> 00:04:01.741
so that through the windows,
you can see it.

00:04:01.741 --> 00:04:05.077
And, in New York City, believe
it or not, you need a stamp.

00:04:05.077 --> 00:04:07.180
Which, a lot of people
will probably be like,

00:04:07.180 --> 00:04:10.182
"Are you kidding me?
I don't have a stamp."

00:04:10.182 --> 00:04:12.752
It's all -- I feel bad.

00:04:12.752 --> 00:04:14.753
I go like, "If there's
someone in their 80s,

00:04:14.753 --> 00:04:16.788
how would you even understand
how to do this,

00:04:16.788 --> 00:04:18.624
unless you have someone
in your family helping you?"

00:04:18.624 --> 00:04:19.925
It's like,
"Wait. This envelope --"

00:04:19.925 --> 00:04:22.161
So I did a video. It's online.

00:04:22.161 --> 00:04:24.196
I show people how easy it is.
-Oh, good!

00:04:24.196 --> 00:04:27.066
-You can do it. And I showed --
This is exactly how do you it.

00:04:27.066 --> 00:04:28.868
You put this envelope
in this thing.

00:04:28.868 --> 00:04:30.736
It's like -- It's possible.
It's good.

00:04:30.736 --> 00:04:32.738
But someone needs
to talk you through it.

00:04:32.738 --> 00:04:34.640
-Yeah.
Sometimes, you know --

00:04:34.640 --> 00:04:37.844
'Cause each state has different
methods, et cetera, et cetera.

00:04:37.844 --> 00:04:40.746
So it's important to decide
what your voting plan is

00:04:40.746 --> 00:04:42.281
and then get it done.

00:04:42.281 --> 00:04:43.616
And if you can early vote,

00:04:43.616 --> 00:04:45.117
like you did
and like I'm going to do,

00:04:45.117 --> 00:04:46.719
that's a very good thing, too.

00:04:46.719 --> 00:04:50.222
'Cause voter turnout
is HUGE this year.

00:04:50.222 --> 00:04:53.092
5 million people have already
voted in Texas. That's a lot.

00:04:53.092 --> 00:04:55.428
-Have they always --
Texas is giant.

00:04:55.428 --> 00:04:57.830
But, I mean, have they always
had a lot of voter turnout,

00:04:57.830 --> 00:05:00.432
or is it just this year?
-No. No.

00:05:00.432 --> 00:05:04.203
They're getting more people
to turn out this year.

00:05:04.203 --> 00:05:07.907
And this year,
there are about 2. million more

00:05:07.907 --> 00:05:12.878
eligible voters in Texas
since 2016.

00:05:12.878 --> 00:05:14.814
So that's like --
That's like the population

00:05:14.814 --> 00:05:16.616
of New Mexico inside of Texas.

00:05:16.616 --> 00:05:18.785
So it's just -- it's just --

00:05:18.785 --> 00:05:20.853
It's a real opportunity.
Let's put it that way.

00:05:20.853 --> 00:05:22.388
-Well, I gotta say,
you have been --

00:05:22.388 --> 00:05:24.757
You said that you were going to
do this and get people to vote.

00:05:24.757 --> 00:05:26.826
And already,
we're seeing numbers go up.

00:05:26.826 --> 00:05:29.328
So this is all because
of everyone's hard work.

00:05:29.328 --> 00:05:31.196
But thank you for doing
all this hard work.

00:05:31.196 --> 00:05:33.131
It's awesome what you are doing.
-Thank you.

00:05:33.131 --> 00:05:36.202
-It's always great to see you.
Good luck with everything

00:05:36.202 --> 00:05:39.472
at the "Fundraiser
About Something."

00:05:39.472 --> 00:05:41.774
-Right.
FundraiserAboutSomething.com.

00:05:41.774 --> 00:05:44.377
Or you can come to my social
and sign up.

00:05:44.377 --> 00:05:46.045
And any amount.
You can give any amount.

00:05:46.045 --> 00:05:47.146
-Yeah.
-Any amount.

00:05:47.146 --> 00:05:48.680
-Love it.
Julia Louis-Dreyfus, everybody.

00:05:48.680 --> 00:05:50.316
We'll be right back
with Patton Oswalt.

00:05:50.316 --> 00:05:51.584
-Thank you.
-You're the best.

00:05:51.584 --> 00:05:53.085
Come back whenever.
-Patton Oswalt!

00:05:53.085 --> 00:05:55.354
Tell him I said hey.
-I will. Perfect.

00:05:55.354 --> 00:05:57.356
-All right.
-Bye.

00:05:57.356 --> 00:05:58.591
-Bye!

